    {
      "id": "vKEsyHFk/XppR9owz#BT60n3Ki",
      "title": "One catalogue defines the surface",
      "narrative": "Every command this CLI has is a row of one table, with the contract that says what it takes. Nothing is registered anywhere else, so help, routing and execution cannot disagree about what exists. Inside another archboard checkout, the entry point first hands the command to that checkout's own bin/archboard, so a worktree runs its own source against its own server. Then it takes --url out, because the modules that talk to the server read its address as they load.",
