    {
      "id": "vKEsyHFk/XppR9owz#Mr26GVEr",
      "title": "Persistence stays in the server",
      "narrative": "No command writes a vault file. Board operations go through the board client, claims and panes through theirs, and the server launcher answers for health; all of them reach the Archboard server as JSON over HTTP through the request transport. The server owns the file, the lease and the version check. What the CLI keeps itself is this machine's list of repository checkouts.",
