    {
      "id": "vKEsyHFk/XppR9owz#tHI5I16e",
      "title": "Three commands draw for themselves",
      "narrative": "Rasterize asks the Archboard server for the SVG like every other command, then photographs it in a headless browser of its own. Record hands a walkthrough to the recorder: the server's own page plays it while the Codex voice narrates, and the recorder keeps that talk. A second browser then draws the talk frame by frame, and ffmpeg makes the video file. Replay renders a kept talk again, with no voice.",
